<sceneDescriptionText>
This is the scene description. It can contain variables, if statements and the like. However, you should not include any method calls that ##
change the game's state here such as arousal changes or money increases. This is because this text is processed every time the "Describe Scene" ##
button is pressed, so those method calls could get processed many times. 
Of course this might be helpful for testing by e.g letting you gradually increase the PC's arousal or whatever, ##
but final submitted content shouldn't have any game effects in the scene description.
</sceneDescriptionText>

<returnFromMakeoutText>
You return from your makeout. Here we have an example of a simple if statement based on what happened in the sub-scene. 

#if($scene.hasFlag("MO_REJECTION"))
Seems that you gave him quite the painful rejection. Poor $m.name. 

We'd better remove the flag so it isn't still set if you make out with him again and choose a different result.
$scene.removeFlag("MO_REJECTION")
#elseif ($m.hadOrgasm)
Looks like $m.name had fun. Lucky him!
#else
Well, you didn't get $m.name off, but you didn't have to tell him to get lost. So there's that.
#end
</returnFromMakeoutText>

<introText>
Hi, this is an example scene written to demonstrate how to make custom scenes in Newlife. I'll be adding to it over time based on feedback from writers and as the custom scene options develop.

This scene has 3 characters. The player character $w.name, a male NPC named $m.name and a female one named $f.name 
</introText>

