<actionWithNpcActionsText>
This action allows an NPC action to be taken. One will be chosen from the list of available ones based on its weight. In this scene you're ##
more likely to see action 1 than action 2.
</actionWithNpcActionsText>

<returnToParentText>
This action returns to the parent scene. This is an alternative to finishScene for sub-scenes that should go back to whatever scene called them, ##
such as a date rather than ending the scene chain.

Under normal circumstances you should not have both returnToParent and finishScene in the same scene. I'm doing it here because this is an example ##
scene, but you should avoid it in your own writing.

When calling this from the test scene, you'll be returned back to it. This lets you run the scene again for further testing. The YML and text file are ##
re-loaded each time you start a scene, so you can make changes to them between test runs
</returnToParentText>

